@taneem-ibrahim @ParBproject, addressed in `19b724a`. the shared validator now uses `urlsplit(api_url).path`, which keeps `;foo` in the path and rejects it while still accepting query parameters and fragments. removed the additional test file; the pr now changes one production file.

reran 16 native completion/chat benchmark cases against the cpu model server: all passed, including local rejection of the semicolon paths. valid cases retained the same generated output and token counts. the existing 23 sweep tests, 80 direct url checks, and pre-commit also passed. the pr description has the updated results and runtime details.

@ywang96, could you re-review and add `verified` if this looks good so upstream pre-commit can run?

